# Coverage floor for the whole project; read by scripts/diff-coverage.sh.
# It can only GO UP: below this number the gate fails, above it the script warns so it can be
# raised in the same commit. The goal is 100% of the DIFF and of the whole, and the whole is
# measured here so a PR that touches no code cannot erode it unnoticed.
#
# 100.00 MEASURED, NOT A TARGET: scripts/diff-coverage.sh prints the total and the list of
# uncovered blocks on every run, so a floor of 100 names whatever falls instead of hiding it
# behind a decimal. Local and CI must both read 100.00 — the suite does not depend on what is
# installed (a fake fd) nor on a live database (the seams in internal/cli), which is what
# makes the number the same in both.
100.00
